> I'm not sure what "intent scrutiny" means. I think "lanli" might be
> better than catlu/zgana for "scrutinize".
>
> "Intense scrutiny" could be "lo nu carmi lo ka lanli".
>
Reading your question as "intense scrutiny" but with the desire to use the 
"inspects" interpretation of catlu for baby-words purposes, I'd imagine 
{tsali catlu} or {denmi catlu} would make sense, though if there is not a 
particular emphasis on the type of sensing, {lanli fi lo nu zgana} or 
similar definitely makes more sense to me.

({.i ta'o}, if the {denmo} bothers you, it bothers me too -- I was looking 
for a word for "focus", but {denmo} is as close as I could get. Given, 
{denmo jundi} makes a lot of sense to me.)

mu'o mi'e .djandus.
 

